    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15829" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ens</span></b> , entis, n.
		sum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				thing;</i> formed, like essentia, after the Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐσία</span>, by Flavius (or Fabianus), acc.
			to <i><span class="en">Quint.
				8, 3, 33</span></i> Spald. <i>N. cr.</i>, but first
			used by Caesar, acc. to <i><span class="en">Prisc. 18, 8,
			75</span></i>: entia (= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰὄντα</span>),
				<i><span class="en">Quint. 2, 14, 2</span></i>.</div>
